{
  "schemaVersion": 4,
  "id": "t07-016",
  "track": "track-07",
  "title": "CSS selectors at-rules cascade values and box model",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "CSS is a declarative language: rules associate selectors with declarations and the browser computes a cascade before layout and paint.",
    "The cascade filters declarations by relevance, origin and importance, layer order, specificity, scoping proximity, and source order, then resolves inheritance and values.",
    "Selectors match elements and pseudo-elements; combinators express relationships, while pseudo-classes express state and structure.",
    "At-rules change stylesheet structure or attach conditions and metadata around style rules; descriptors configure some at-rules.",
    "The box model determines content, padding, border, and margin geometry; box-sizing controls how declared dimensions map to that geometry.",
    "CSS values move through declared, cascaded, specified, computed, used, and actual stages; functions, types, and units form their syntax."
  ],
